<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Abkhaz SSR</h1><p class="st-meta">1921 CE – 1931 CE · capital Sukhumi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Soviet republic of Abkhazia that existed from 1921 to 1931 in a treaty union with Georgia, a status later invoked by Abkhaz separatists.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> overthrew the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/democratic-republic-of-georgia">Democratic Republic of Georgia</a> in early 1921, Bolsheviks at Sukhumi proclaimed the Soviet Socialist Republic of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-abkhazia">Abkhazia</a> on 31 March 1921. In December 1921 it signed a special union treaty with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgian-ssr">Georgian SSR</a>, and through it joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/transcaucasian-sfsr">Transcaucasian SFSR</a> in 1922.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was led by the popular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abkhaz-people">Abkhaz</a> Bolshevik <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nestor-lakoba">Nestor Lakoba</a>, who slowed collectivisation and protected local landowners and traditions. It had its own constitution from 1925 and promoted the Abkhaz language and culture, while its economy rested on tobacco, citrus fruit and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> resorts.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1931, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-stalin">Stalin</a>, its status was reduced to that of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abkhaz-people">Abkhaz</a> Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgian-ssr">Georgian SSR</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nestor-lakoba">Lakoba</a> died in 1936, probably poisoned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lavrentiy-beria">Beria</a>. Abkhaz leaders cited the 1921-1931 republic when breaking away from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgia">Georgia</a> in the 1990s.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/abkhaz-ssr.jpg" alt="Abkhaz SSR" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Himasaram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_SSR_Abkhazia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1921 CE – 1931 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sukhumi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nestor Lakoba</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity and Sunni Islam (officially atheist state)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Abkhaz; Russian; Georgian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/georgia">Georgia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Socialist Soviet Republic of Abkhazia, SSR Abkhazia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=abkhaz-ssr" aria-label="Abkhaz SSR on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5670 651 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Abkhaz SSR lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5990 907L6091 947"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6091 947h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5990 907h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5990 907h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=abkhaz-ssr">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
